# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# IDE
.idea/

# Claude Code worktrees (isolated checkouts)
.claude/worktrees/

# Stop-hook ack latches (per-session, wt_stop_check.sh)
.claude/wt-status/

# NOTE: python-hslog/ is TRACKED. It used to be gitignored, which meant a
# clone lacked the parser while the release zip had it — the spin-out into
# this repo made the repo and the release the same tree, so it is vendored
# properly now (upstream's own tests, which carry third-party BattleTags,
# are not vendored).

# Regenerable caches — downloaded card data, rebuilt by the tools here
# (parse_minions.py --refresh-tribes, scrape_comps.py, patch_day.py)
#
# Basenames, NOT `meta/...`: these patterns kept a `meta/` prefix when the code
# moved into app/ (fbd2920) and a pattern with a slash is anchored to the root,
# so they silently stopped matching `app/meta/...`. The 2026-10-04 refresh
# surfaced it — `git status` showed the trinket caches as untracked in a tree
# where `sync.py --new` commits untracked files. A bare basename matches at any
# depth, which is why `.cards_cache.json` survived the move and these did not.
.cards_cache.json
.cards_full.json
.observed_tribes.json
.trinkets_hsjson_cache.json
.trinkets_guides_cache.json

# On-demand art fetch failures (coach_ui), regenerable
.art_miss.json

# Per-user advisory telemetry (the beta corpus pairs these with Power.logs)
decision_logs/

# The user's sharing answer, and the distilled reports this install has sent
# (session_reports/ holds a local copy of everything shared plus the per-session
# id map). Local state, never a source of truth, and the one kind of file this
# project must never commit by accident: `git add -A` took the id map as
# untracked before this line existed (2026-10-03).
.share_consent.json
session_reports/

# Where THIS machine was told Hearthstone lives, written by `config.py --set`
# when the game is not in the usual place (2026-10-06). Machine-specific, so it
# must not be committed — and `sync.py --new` commits untracked files, which is
# how a bare basename pattern here matters more than it looks: a pattern with a
# slash is anchored to the root and stops matching once the file is written
# under app/ (the fbd2920 mistake, one line up in this file's history).
.hs_home.json

# The release signing key: the Ed25519 PRIVATE key the publisher keeps offline.
# It has no business in this repo, in a release zip, or anywhere near Cloudflare,
# and `sync.py --new` commits untracked files — which is why the basename guard
# matters here more than it looks. Its public half is pinned in
# app/release_sig.py (PUBKEY_B64), and the private half is what the whole update
# channel's trust now rests on (2026-10-07).
.bobs-ledger-release.key
release_signing_key

# Saved game reviews (the Settle Up tab's store, app/saved_replays/): one
# JSON per game the player chose to keep. Per-user data, the same class as
# decision_logs/ — basename pattern, for the sync.py --new reason above.
saved_replays/

# Where fetch_sessions.py puts reports it pulls back from the collector. That is
# OTHER PEOPLE'S data — the beta testers' decisions — landing in a git tree, and
# this directory was neither ignored nor mentioned in publish_release's
# exclusions until 2026-10-04, while the tool's own default is to write it here.
# `sync.py --new` commits untracked files, so the failure mode is a push.
sessions_in/

# Packaged corpus bundles awaiting upload
corpus_out/

# Local Power.log archives and generated patch-check artifacts
logs_archive/
patch_reports/
.patch_state.json
.patch_config.json

# Automation caches (logquery/review_kit): regenerable, machine-specific
.review_cache/

# comp_miner proposals: derived from the local log corpus (which is not in the
# repo), regenerable, and never a source of truth — promotion is a human edit
# to meta/comps.json. NOTE: this one was already committed to the repo before
# the `meta/` prefix stopped matching (app/meta/comp_candidates.json is tracked);
# it does not ship (publish_release EXCLUDE_FILES), but untracking it is a
# decision for the maintainer, not a side effect of fixing the pattern.
comp_candidates.json

# YouTube auto-transcripts (third-party caption text, takedown bait):
# derived research cache — mined into the guides, never republished.
transcripts/

# The card->tribe map is downloaded from HearthstoneJSON, but it SHIPS inside
# every release so a first run needs no network (bans._load_card_races reads
# it before it would ever fetch). Gitignored because it is regenerable;
# publish_release.py lists it in UNTRACKED_OK so it still ships.
.card_races.json

# A built release zip is an artifact, not a source file
bobs-ledger-*.zip

# Per-install stamps: VERSION is written by publish_release.py into each zip,
# .update_state.json by update.py on apply. A stale local copy must not be
# committed or shipped.
VERSION
.update_state.json

# The staging area update.py uses while installing a release. It exists only on
# an install that is mid-update (or was interrupted mid-update) and carries the
# replaced copies a rollback restores. Never a source of truth, never shipped.
.staging/

# Wrangler local state — carries the CF account id / account email
.wrangler/
telemetry/.wrangler/
.dev.vars
*.env

# Local API-key bootstrap helper (never ships, never commits)
claude_code_zai_env.sh

# Scratch dirs used while verifying a release build
.tmp_*/

# Shortcuts: created by the launcher on the machine that uses them, and they
# embed absolute paths — never committed, never shipped (publish_release.py
# excludes *.lnk too, since it walks the working tree rather than git).
*.lnk
